# Coconut Leaf Disease Detection — ML Pipeline Overview

## 1. Problem Statement

Detect and classify **4 types of coconut leaf diseases** from images using object detection:

| Class ID | Disease | Description |
|---|---|---|
| 0 | **Caterpillar** | Caterpillar damage + caterpillar spots (merged) |
| 1 | **Drying** | Leaf drying/browning |
| 2 | **Flaccidity** | Wilting/drooping leaves |
| 3 | **Yellowing** | Chlorosis/yellowing of leaves |

---

## 2. ML Model & Architecture

### Model: **YOLOv8m** (You Only Look Once v8 — Medium)

| Property | Value |
|---|---|
| Framework | [Ultralytics YOLOv8](https://docs.ultralytics.com/) (v8.4.17) |
| Variant | **YOLOv8m** (Medium) |
| Parameters | **25.86M** (25,858,636 total, 25,858,620 trainable) |
| GFLOPs | **79.1** |
| Layers | 170 |
| Architecture | C2f + SPPF + PAN-FPN + Detect Head |
| Task | Object Detection (bounding box + class) |
| Pretrained On | COCO dataset (80 classes) → Fine-tuned to 4 classes |

### Architecture Breakdown

```mermaid
graph TD
    A[Input Image 640×640×3] --> B[Backbone]
    B --> C[Neck PAN-FPN]
    C --> D[Detection Head]
    D --> E[Bounding Boxes + Class Predictions]
    
    subgraph "Backbone (Feature Extraction)"
        B1[Conv 3→48] --> B2[Conv 48→96]
        B2 --> B3[C2f ×2 96ch]
        B3 --> B4[Conv 96→192]
        B4 --> B5[C2f ×4 192ch]
        B5 --> B6[Conv 192→384]
        B6 --> B7[C2f ×4 384ch]
        B7 --> B8[Conv 384→576]
        B8 --> B9[C2f ×2 576ch]
        B9 --> B10[SPPF 576ch]
    end
    
    subgraph "Neck (Multi-scale Feature Fusion)"
        N1[Upsample + Concat] --> N2[C2f 384ch]
        N2 --> N3[Upsample + Concat]
        N3 --> N4[C2f 192ch — P3]
        N4 --> N5[Conv + Concat]
        N5 --> N6[C2f 384ch — P4]
        N6 --> N7[Conv + Concat]
        N7 --> N8[C2f 576ch — P5]
    end
    
    subgraph "Head (Multi-scale Detection)"
        H1[Detect P3 — Small objects]
        H2[Detect P4 — Medium objects]
        H3[Detect P5 — Large objects]
    end
```

### Key Architecture Components

| Component | Purpose |
|---|---|
| **C2f** (Cross-Stage Partial with 2 convolutions) | Efficient feature extraction with gradient flow |
| **SPPF** (Spatial Pyramid Pooling - Fast) | Multi-scale context aggregation |
| **PAN-FPN** (Path Aggregation + Feature Pyramid) | Multi-scale feature fusion for detecting objects at different sizes |
| **Detect Head** | 3-scale detection (P3/P4/P5) with decoupled class + box regression |
| **DFL** (Distribution Focal Loss) | Better bounding box regression via learned distributions |

---

## 3. Algorithm & Loss Functions

### Detection Algorithm
- **Anchor-Free Detection**: YOLOv8 is anchor-free — it directly predicts object centers and box dimensions, unlike earlier YOLO versions
- **Non-Maximum Suppression (NMS)**: Post-processing to remove duplicate detections (IoU threshold = 0.45)
- **Multi-Scale**: Detects at 3 feature map scales (P3, P4, P5) for objects of varying sizes

### Loss Functions (3 components combined)

| Loss | Purpose | Weight |
|---|---|---|
| **Box Loss** (CIoU) | Bounding box regression accuracy | 7.5 |
| **Classification Loss** (BCE) | Class prediction accuracy | 0.5 |
| **DFL Loss** (Distribution Focal) | Fine-grained box boundary prediction | 1.5 |

### Optimization

| Setting | Value |
|---|---|
| Optimizer | **AdamW** (Adam with decoupled weight decay) |
| Initial Learning Rate | **0.001** |
| Final Learning Rate | 0.001 × 0.01 = **0.00001** |
| LR Schedule | **Cosine Annealing** (smooth decay) |
| Weight Decay | 0.0005 |
| Warmup | 3 epochs (LR ramp from 0 → 0.001) |
| Early Stopping | Patience = 15 epochs |

---

## 4. Dataset

### Source & Format

| Property | Value |
|---|---|
| Source | **Roboflow** (COCO JSON format) |
| Converted To | **YOLO format** ([.txt](file:///d:/M3%20Projects/Coconut_Leaf_Disease_Detection/backend/cookies.txt) label files with normalized bboxes) |
| Image Resolution | Variable (resized to 640×640 during training) |

### Dataset Splits

| Split | Images | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| **Train** | 726 | Model training |
| **Validation** | 223 | Epoch-end evaluation & early stopping |
| **Test** | 104 | Final evaluation (untouched during training) |
| **Total** | **1,053** | |

### Original → Final Class Mapping

The original dataset had 7 categories. These were consolidated into 4 disease classes:

| Original (COCO ID) | Action | Final (YOLO ID) |
|---|---|---|
| 0: coconut-leaves | ❌ **Skipped** (supercategory, 0 annotations) | — |
| 1: caterpillar | ✅ **Kept** | 0: caterpillar |
| 2: caterpillar-spot | 🔀 **Merged** into caterpillar | 0: caterpillar |
| 3: drying | ✅ **Kept** | 1: drying |
| 4: finger | ❌ **Skipped** (not a disease) | — |
| 5: flaccidity | ✅ **Kept** | 2: flaccidity |
| 6: yellowing | ✅ **Kept** | 3: yellowing |

---

## 5. Data Pipeline

### Step-by-step Flow

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    A["📁 Raw Dataset<br/>Roboflow COCO JSON"] --> B["🔄 convert_coco_to_yolo.py<br/>Class merging & remapping"]
    B --> C["📂 YOLO Format<br/>images/ & labels/"]
    C --> D["🧠 train.py<br/>YOLOv8 Training"]
    D --> E["💾 best.pt<br/>Trained Weights"]
    E --> F["🔍 inference.py<br/>Prediction"]
    E --> G["📊 evaluate.py<br/>Evaluation"]
    E --> H["🌐 app.py<br/>Flask API"]
```

### Annotation Conversion ([convert_coco_to_yolo.py](file:///d:/M3%20Projects/Coconut_Leaf_Disease_Detection/ml/src/convert_coco_to_yolo.py))

1. Reads [_annotations.coco.json](file:///d:/M3%20Projects/Coconut_Leaf_Disease_Detection/ml/datasets/Coconut%20Leaf%20Pest%20Detection/train/_annotations.coco.json) from each split
2. Merges `caterpillar` + `caterpillar-spot` → class 0
3. Skips `finger` annotations (class 4) and `coconut-leaves` (class 0)
4. Converts bboxes: `[x_min, y_min, w, h]` (pixels) → `[cx, cy, w, h]` (normalized)
5. Clamps all values to `[0, 1]`
6. Writes per-image [.txt](file:///d:/M3%20Projects/Coconut_Leaf_Disease_Detection/backend/cookies.txt) label files

---

## 6. Training Configuration

### Current Settings ([config.yaml](file:///d:/M3%20Projects/Coconut_Leaf_Disease_Detection/ml/src/config.yaml))

#### Training Hyperparameters

| Parameter | Value | Description |
|---|---|---|
| Epochs | 100 | Maximum training epochs |
| Batch Size | 8 | Limited by 6GB VRAM |
| Image Size | 640×640 | Input resolution |
| Patience | 15 | Early stop if no mAP improvement |
| Optimizer | AdamW | Adam with weight decay |
| LR₀ | 0.001 | Initial learning rate |
| LR_f | 0.01 × LR₀ | Final learning rate ratio |
| Warmup | 3 epochs | Gradual LR ramp-up |
| Cosine LR | ✅ | Smooth LR decay schedule |
| Workers | 2 | DataLoader workers (limited for Windows) |

#### Data Augmentation

| Augmentation | Value | Effect |
|---|---|---|
| HSV-Hue | 0.015 | Slight color shift |
| HSV-Saturation | 0.7 | Color intensity variation |
| HSV-Value | 0.4 | Brightness variation |
| Rotation | ±10° | Moderate rotation |
| Translation | 10% | Slight position shift |
| Scale | 0.5 | Zoom in/out variation |
| Horizontal Flip | 50% | Left-right mirror |
| Vertical Flip | 0% | Disabled (leaves have orientation) |
| Mosaic | 100% | Combines 4 images into 1 |
| Mixup | 10% | Blends 2 images together |
| Copy-Paste | 0% | Disabled |

---

## 7. Training Pipeline ([train.py](file:///d:/M3%20Projects/Coconut_Leaf_Disease_Detection/ml/src/train.py))

### Execution Flow

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A[Start train.py] --> B[Load config.yaml]
    B --> C[Set up TeeLogger<br/>Console + file logging]
    C --> D[Parse CLI arguments<br/>epochs, batch, resume]
    D --> E{Resume?}
    E -->|Yes| F[Load last.pt checkpoint]
    E -->|No| G[Load pretrained yolov8m.pt]
    F --> H[Override nc=4]
    G --> H
    H --> I[Register epoch callback<br/>on_fit_epoch_end]
    I --> J[🚀 model.train<br/>with all hyperparameters]
    J --> K[Training loop<br/>100 epochs max]
    K --> L{Early stopping?<br/>patience=15}
    L -->|No improvement| M[Stop training]
    L -->|Improving| K
    M --> N[Copy best.pt to weights/]
    N --> O[Print training summary table]
    O --> P[Save results & plots]
```

### Key Features
- **Real-time logging**: [TeeLogger](file:///d:/M3%20Projects/Coconut_Leaf_Disease_Detection/ml/src/train.py#28-86) captures all output to both console and timestamped log files
- **Epoch summary callback**: Prints a clean one-line summary after each epoch with all key metrics
- **Automatic best model saving**: Copies `best.pt` to the weights directory
- **Training summary table**: Generates a per-epoch results table at the end

---

